<body>
    <h1>Firm Relationships Overview</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"contentLayout2">
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><span style=3D"font-size: 14.0px;letter-spacing: 0.0px;">This page o=
utlines the business relationships an independent wealth management firm ma=
y have to run their business.&nbsp; </span><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0=
.0px;font-size: 14.0px;">Canada=E2=80=99s baseline registration architectur=
e is set by the CSA=E2=80=99s NI 31-103, while CIRO governs investment deal=
ers and mutual fund dealers, and additional rules apply if the firm also op=
erates investment funds or insurance/planning channels.&nbsp; Additionally =
</span><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;font-size: 14.0px;">NI 81-102 r=
egulates publicly offered investment funds, such as mutual funds.</span></p=
>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"FirmRelationshipsOverview-Background:FirmRelationships">Backg=
round: Firm Relationships</h1>
    <p>An independent wealth management firm relies on a network of externa=
l relationships because it cannot efficiently perform every required functi=
on itself=E2=80=94from holding client assets and accessing markets to manuf=
acturing products and meeting compliance obligations. These relationships a=
llow the firm to leverage specialized providers (e.g., custodians, brokers,=
 sub-advisers, distributors, and technology vendors), extend its service of=
fering through professional partners, and maintain appropriate governance a=
nd oversight.</p>
    <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"451" style=3D"width:451=
px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"cabc420afb37a53903cf0d8eefe6f39afc4ed4cc28dbac2=
b9cca3bd9df651965" height=3D"410"></p>
    <p><span style=3D"font-size: 20.0px;letter-spacing: -0.16px;">Definitio=
ns</span></p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 84.4493%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 9.45469%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 11.1577%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 29.4799%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 49.9151%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Type</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Term</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Definition</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Key Characteristics&nbsp;<=
/th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td rowspan=3D"3" class=3D"confluenceTd">Hierarchal</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">(Registered) Firm</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">An independently registered company&nbsp=
;/ entity (with regulators)</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"1312adc5-3409-4384-aecc-89ac57267f36">Owns the i=
nvestor relationship (incl KYC, KYP, suitability, conflicts, disclosure obl=
igations under NI 31-103), full service offering, and business operations</=
li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Parent Firm</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A multi-firm/entity business that has on=
e or more firms</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"94c10647-8ad1-483f-b1ab-2be38b20d542">A business=
 that offers multiple registered business models, such as both an advice an=
d discretionary channel, or fund management in addition to portfolio manage=
ment</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Child Firm</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A registered firm that is owned by a par=
ent company or a parent group</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"39492098-7bfb-4395-a45d-875116a62970">May be ful=
ly independent operated or partially centralized depending on various facto=
rs</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td rowspan=3D"3" class=3D"confluenceTd">Partnerships &amp; Outsour=
cing (Delegation)</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Sub-Advisor</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A firm that has entered into a sub-advis=
ory or delegated portfolio management agreement with a parent or child firm=
 to manage portfolios on behalf of the firm</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"97889be8-ef43-4839-8b1e-97e9fd89af01">These are =
registered PM firms who manage all or part of a strategy, sleeve, model, ma=
ndate, geography, or asset class of their client firm</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"ad96d424-0b17-4ff9-8493-23cbbc89e3c3"><span styl=
e=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Responsible for trading within the delegated a=
ccounts of their client firm</span></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"eee81336-cdd5-4851-b531-1973953ea1e4">These firm=
s can be clients or non-clients of NBIN</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Referral Agent</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A firm that has a referral arrangement i=
n place with a parent or child firm to offer services that can range from p=
roviding client name &amp; contact, to financial services and investment pr=
oducts and will include a referral fee.&nbsp; This is one of the most commo=
n relationships in wealth management.</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"a167164b-2ca2-458c-88a3-323731097eef">Typically =
includes sharing or splitting commissions resulting in securities transacti=
ons, or fee payment for client onboarding</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"e35a21be-832e-42d9-a5cc-837dbb7a917c">Disclosure=
s need to be provided to clients typically by the registered firm</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"005d6cfd-aa50-4167-aa2f-a8fb45d72cdd">Lending / =
credit not permitted to limit financial exposure of a registered firm</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"2464afea-076a-487d-8add-9a4f080c70a6">These firm=
s can be clients or non-clients of NBIN</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Fund Manager</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A registered investment fund manager who=
 creates pooled funds or purchasing</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"1c0f31cc-04a6-4deb-9b1e-6c3eb53c805b">IFM's are =
responsible for the fund's administration, governance and compliance</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"6728e541-7348-4d09-a99c-2d83cbf4a056">A mutual f=
und / investment dealer may choose to establish a distribution relationship=
 with a fund manager to sell their funds&nbsp;</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"470911a5-5bec-4a54-9078-b566dff9a0fd">More commo=
nly, PM's are moving towards creating pooled funds to be 'purchased' into t=
heir discretionary client accounts to simplify their operations</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"fc34d345-4fb8-4010-918e-3eccc744296c"><span>It i=
s very rare (we have 2) to have IFM without PM since distribution is challe=
nging - in the case of a PM/IFM under the same holding company, this is a h=
ierarchal relationship NOT an outsourcing relationship</span></li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td rowspan=3D"2" class=3D"confluenceTd">Services Providers</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Fund Operations</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Secondary relationships required for the Fund Manager to effect=
ively operate a fund.&nbsp; This can include fund administrators, auditors,=
 accountants, trustees, etc.</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"9edfce16-f5d8-4d1d-bd08-d4b7a54ea62a">Activities=
 can include e.g. for fund administrators, calculating NAV, maintain unitho=
lder records, process subscriptions/redemptions, prepare reports and suppor=
t operations</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Professional collaboration</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Companies that a parent or child firm ma=
y contract for wealth-adjacent services, such as insurance, planning, trust=
, accounting, technology, etc.</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"c4ae1ffa-3f3e-4a54-a5ba-ddf57de5fe15">Typically =
requires sharing of essential client and investment information&nbsp;</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Other</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">?? Ghost firms</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Parent firms that are not actual entitie=
s but are specifically there in order for NBIN to utilize the grouping for =
aggregated reporting purposes. Ghost parent firms do not have users nor acc=
ounts.</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Current state; ghost parent firms do not=
 have any contracts signed with NBIN. Any contracts are signed with the ind=
ividual child firms of the ghost parent firm.</td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"FirmRelationshipsOverview-FirmRelationshipScenarios">Firm Rel=
ationship Scenarios</h1>
    <p>Understanding these relationships are critical because they define h=
ow client assets, transactions, data, and responsibilities flow across the =
broader wealth ecosystem.&nbsp;</p>
    <p>Independent firms rely on us as the operational backbone for safekee=
ping, settlement, reporting, and regulatory recordkeeping, which means we s=
it at the center of a complex network of upstream (advisors, IFMs, sub-advi=
sers) and downstream (clients, regulators, tax authorities) interactions.&n=
bsp; As a result, understanding and supporting these relationships is essen=
tial to designing scalable digital capabilities =E2=80=94 such as onboardin=
g workflows, data integration, reporting, and APIs =E2=80=94 that can accom=
modate different business models, delegation structures, and regulatory req=
uirements.</p>
    <p>Our digital strategy must therefore be relationship-aware, enabling =
seamless connectivity, transparency, and control across multiple counterpar=
ties, while reinforcing our role as a trusted infrastructure provider withi=
n an increasingly modular and interconnected wealth management value chain.=
</p>
    <p><span style=3D"color:#22a06b;"><strong>Core Use Cases</strong></span=
></p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 93.8161%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 6.50145%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 6.3435%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 2.69572%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 9.19717%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 24.4729%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 31.7672%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 19.0815%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Relationship</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Population</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Scenario</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Description</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Example</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Capability Considerations<=
/th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td rowspan=3D"3" class=3D"confluenceTd">Hierarchy</td>
        <td rowspan=3D"3" class=3D"confluenceTd">85 parents</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#22a06b;"><strong>1=
</strong></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><span style=3D"color:#22a06b;"><strong>Parent =E2=86=92 Child (=
1:N)</strong></span></p>
         <p><br></p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Parent entity / holding company =
with multiple registered firms.&nbsp; <span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;=
">Business and operations across firms are typically overseen at the group =
level.</span></span></p>
         <p>See note below on why these structures exist.</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p>Cumberland, Fiera</p>
          <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"200" style=3D"wid=
th:200px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"ecb23ca067872c72be16b37c392cc62f6a4337028=
0f39e90ff75538ddc821164" height=3D"148"></p>
          <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-emb=
edded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"fa=
lse" height=3D"203" src=3D"469796ea35e496e1d8d7f9d3da301f1754b4715b6e672408=
0300c18769003613" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/2621822086/image-=
2026-4-16_18-16-15.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1780161703410&amp=
;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"2=
743425697" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"=
attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2026-4-16_18-16-15.=
png" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-typ=
e=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2621822086" data-linke=
d-resource-container-version=3D"39" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"><=
/span></p>
         </div></td>
        <td rowspan=3D"2" class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p>Aligns with core CX platform proposition to support the differ=
ent organizational setups of our firms</p>
         </div>
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><br></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#22a06b;"><strong>2=
</strong></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#22a06b;"><strong>C=
hild =E2=86=92 Child with Parent Grouping (N:N)</strong></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Specific case of 1 or 2, where IFM is created to simplify inves=
tment management for the PM arm (and to reduce cost of trading).&nbsp; Vari=
ations:</p>
         <ol>
          <li data-uuid=3D"3b5c49a2-49fa-4410-9922-a6ff0daa403c">PM + IFM -=
 same entity=20
           <ol>
            <li data-uuid=3D"08015c62-dcb1-486c-ac0e-4b9016a799b7">
             <p>Simpler governance and compliance framework</p></li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"d1a45463-55f7-421a-b7ec-215ef39c9377">
             <p>Easier client disclosure / relationship clarity</p></li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"2edc647f-67aa-49b7-af98-ed8a5c82248d">Lower op=
erational overhead</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"e098ee68-3435-4061-9f3c-3536021d0be1">
             <p>Direct control over fund oversight and portfolio management=
</p></li>
           </ol></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"b61fc2c3-087d-49ad-bc29-c5674bc83b51">Separate P=
M entity + separate IFM entity=20
           <ol>
            <li data-uuid=3D"ecc4bc83-1d23-4948-85ab-03b33239a592">Function=
al separation</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"603882c6-1a0f-47c6-98a7-968ee4bc7e96">Liabilit=
y segregation</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"d75bf0ac-1eee-4260-96f2-28116c768afc">Conflict=
 management</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"8bb3b905-18af-4b57-b7d6-9d96daf8e9b7">Business=
 flexibility</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"fa022530-5b8e-49bc-bc8e-7b3b4fbb91ae">Requires=
 formalized intercompany agreements and separate filing, audits</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"e5f4dea5-fd94-4e50-8f3f-2407251d8c59">Each ent=
ity must independently meet registration requirements even if shared person=
nel are used (via service agreements)</li>
           </ol></li>
         </ol></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p>Baskin, Cote100</p>
          <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"400" style=3D"wid=
th:400px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"067f7d8f78b091f0b8611a493560d34a12de2faf0=
e2185f66e10055f8d98aba3" height=3D"84"></p>
          <p><br></p>
          <p>:question: Need examples of each and in the case of #2 do we h=
ave cases where there are truly no "parent" staff.&nbsp; Otherwise assume t=
here is always somebody.</p>
          <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-emb=
edded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"fa=
