         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">3</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Multi-parent (edge case)</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Typically a transitionary use case or edge case where one firm =
may have acquired another but relationship has not been updated in&nbsp;<sp=
an style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Firm360</span></p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p>Harbourfront + KJH (Prior to May 2026)</p>
          <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-emb=
edded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"fa=
lse" width=3D"468" src=3D"009dabac1775f7f960825c3a1b9fbbcd4546541262f8f65d2=
49167f16bc5355a" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/2621822086/image-2=
026-4-16_15-51-48.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1780161733409&amp;=
api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"27=
43425702" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"a=
ttachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2026-4-16_15-51-48.p=
ng" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=
=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2621822086" data-linked=
-resource-container-version=3D"39" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" height=3D"237"><=
/span></p>
          <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-emb=
edded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"fa=
lse" width=3D"468" src=3D"3e06417f00a99839201271bdf64c1cb96a747abdd8a1986d9=
e1dcc1a17b5dcea" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/2621822086/image-2=
026-4-16_18-21-6.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1780161733903&amp;a=
pi=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"274=
3425703" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"at=
tachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2026-4-16_18-21-6.png=
" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=
=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2621822086" data-linked=
-resource-container-version=3D"39" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" height=3D"129"><=
/span></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Must consider how we may facilitate modification and transition=
 of firms when their hierarchy changes</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td rowspan=3D"2" class=3D"confluenceTd">Delegation</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">45 sub-advisors to 35 firms</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#22a06b;"><strong>4=
</strong></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#22a06b;"><strong>F=
irm =E2=86=92 Partner within NBIN network&nbsp;<span>(1:N)</span></strong><=
/span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Firms can have 1 or more sub-advisors, and sub-advisors can ser=
vice 1 or more firms.&nbsp; <span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Sub-advi=
sors are onboarded onto firm's specific account ranges that need to be serv=
iced.</span></p>
         <p>We should see less of these relationships as the trend is to tr=
ansition into pooled fund purchasing to simplify transactions and client ho=
ldings.</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Guardian, Mawer</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Should ensure the ability for a firm to manage accesses of thei=
r providers and ideally easily identify them as such</p>
         <p>Access management includes assignment of specific views and cap=
abilities as determined by the firm, which will be based on the nature of t=
he agreement or <span>arrangement.</span></p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;">Unknown</=
span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;">5</span><=
/td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;">Firm -&gt=
; Partner outside NBIN network</span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;">Difficult=
 to tell since they are typically onboarded as employees of the firm</span>=
</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>It is less critical to resolve the outsourcing partner experien=
ce especially for non-firms of NBIN.&nbsp; There is low demand currently to=
 address frictions from these firms unless they are impacting the efficienc=
y of NBIN clients.</p>
         <p>However, operationally it may be more manageable to identify an=
d govern an individual's 360 access&nbsp;</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Combo</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">TBC</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#22a06b;"><strong>6=
</strong></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#22a06b;"><strong>P=
arent =E2=86=92 child =E2=86=92 sub-advisor</strong></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p>Combination of hierarchal and outsourcing relationship</p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p>Wellington - Guardian</p>
          <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"400" style=3D"wid=
th:400px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"864863497b2a515270a0a2fb9c5c56ea53c6cc42c=
af71b3fecddfa7237b72c5e" height=3D"170"></p>
          <p>:question: Assumes parent company governs use of outsourcing p=
artners</p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><br></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td rowspan=3D"2" class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#8590=
a2;">Service providers</span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Unknown</=
span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;"><span sty=
le=3D"color:#8590a2;">7</span></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Fund admi=
nistrators</span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Firms sho=
uld provision account / data access accordingly</span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">SGGG ~100 users</span></p>
         <p>:question: Confirm if this is our own supplier or individual cl=
ient relationships</p></td>
        <td rowspan=3D"2" class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;"><span>Can be a future considerat=
ion but this category of relationship is 2 degrees removed from NBIN.</span=
></span></p><br><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;">&nbsp;</span></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;">Unknown</=
span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;">8</span><=
/td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;">Technolog=
y supplier</span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;">Firms sho=
uld provision account / data access accordingly</span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#8590a2;">NDEX</spa=
n></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><span style=3D"font-size: 20.0px;letter-spacing: -0.008em;">A Note o=
n Firm360 Hierarchy</span></p>
    <p>There are usually several reasons for grouping two or more individua=
l firms (with a distinct firm identifier) under a parent firm group structu=
re.</p>
    <p><strong>1. Merge &amp; Acquisitions, e.g. Harbourfront</strong></p>
    <p>After a M&amp;A, there are two options:</p>
    <ul>
     <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"82b79aba-f7cd-4d56-b2b0-96e=
c4e575f0c">
      <p>Option A: Account Conversion</p>
      <ul>
       <li class=3D"paragraph-child">
        <p>The firm could choose to convert the client accounts of the acqu=
ired firm(s) to the parent firm, which is essentially "offboarding" the acq=
uired firm(s), dismantling their firm identifiers, broker codes, RR codes a=
nd account ranges.</p></li>
       <li class=3D"paragraph-child">
        <p>However, it would result in a major disruption to end clients (e=
.g. new account number). Besides, as the firm grows, their RR code &amp; ac=
count ranges will grow, too.&nbsp;</p></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"e133e4c7-f77d-40c0-896b-e85=
a9657ea24">
      <p>Option B: Re-branding</p>
      <ul>
       <li class=3D"paragraph-child">
        <p>&nbsp;Alternatively, the firm may choose the re-branding solutio=
n by changing their company logo on website and letterheads only while keep=
ing client account numbers the same. There is no impact to the acquired fir=
ms' firm identifiers, broker codes and RR code/Account ranges.</p></li>
       <li class=3D"paragraph-child">
        <p>This is an easier way to do as the client account numbers remain=
 intact, and it provides a bigger room for growth.</p></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"848f532b-0708-430a-a009-098=
570043251">As a result, Option B is often preferred, however ideally multip=
les of the same business types is not ideal (e.g. multiple IB's, multiple P=
M's)</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>2. Parent group created by NBIN, e.g. PM / IFM that are sepa=
rate entities</strong></p>
    <ul>
     <li class=3D"paragraph-child" data-uuid=3D"ed064e7f-20c0-43e6-a427-d57=
0210d3ce0">
      <p>This is usually requested by NBIN N4 and agreed by Client to group=
ing related firms for P&amp;L purpose.</p></li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>3. Firms with multiple business models</strong></p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"ea2e32c3-38f1-4939-95c8-c9ed694c36cf">Firms that oper=
ates in multiple business models may be setup with multiple registered enti=
ties for ease of segregation, rather than a single entity that holds multip=
le registrations, particularly if they were not investment dealers with dis=
cretionary authority (like IPC or iA)</li>
    </ul>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
